-- title:
--   Affine chart of the descended model, read on given data
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a valuation subring $A\subset\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the symbol $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A` denotes its residue field. Two modular function fields occur: `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the intermediate field of `LaurentSeries` $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (itself the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the series $q$-expansions `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the divisors $d$ of $M'$), and `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. For a field $K$, `modularFunctionFieldC K M'` is the intermediate field of Laurent series generated over $K$ by `jqModC K` and `jqNModC K M'`.
--
--   The supersingular-place data consist of: a prime $q$ with $5\le q$; a natural number $M'$, nonzero, with $q\nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A\subset\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, that is, $q$ is a nonunit of $A$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ whose members are, by `hW`, exactly the elements of `ssPlaces q M' κ` (a place $w$ is such when $w$ is rational, is an affine geometric place, and $w$.`evalAt` of the generator `jGeomGen κ M'` lies in `ssJSet q κ`); the inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` in `fieldBar q M'`; a constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ with residual field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, i.e. a valuation subring $R_0$.`integers` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` cutting out $A$ on constants, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0$.`residue` onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal and compatible with reduction of constants, such that every nonzero element becomes a nonzero residue after scaling by a constant, together with a degree-preserving map $R_0$.`placeMap` on places compatible with divisors of elements of nonzero residue; the hypothesis `hR₀`, which requires that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` that image lies in $R_0$.`integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; and a chosen element $s$ of $W$.
--
--   The small-constant data consist of: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb{Q}\subset\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that the valuation ring $A\cap k_0$ (written as the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hdvr`, `hunif`), is Henselian local (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); the hypothesis `hκ`, that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$; a prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and an element $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   The base layer consists of an intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0\subset\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $K_b=\bot$, a valuation subring $A_b\subset K_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$ (`hAb`), and a nonzero $\varpi_b\in A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through the composite $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`. It asserts: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subset$ `fieldBar q M'` satisfying the four conditions
--   (F1) $f\in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient $f_n$ ($n\in\mathbb{Z}$) of $f$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the image of $k_0$;
--   (F2) the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with $F_0$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`;
--   (F3) $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ in $SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$, where `levelAutBar` is the chosen $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` satisfying the $q$-expansion condition `IsLevelAutBar`, the identity if none exists;
--   (F4) (linear disjointness) for every finite $k_0$-subextension $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces $a_i=0$ for all $i$;
--   and for every valuation subring $W_0\subset F_0$ satisfying the six conditions
--   (W1) for $x\in k_0$: $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$;
--   (W2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring;
--   (W3) the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal;
--   (W4) for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base-changed image $\bar g$ lies in $R_0$.`integers`, if $\bar g$ has nonnegative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which the image of `jq` has nonnegative order, and if $R_0$.`residue` $\bar g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then the image of $\bar g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$, lies in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $A$ equals $s$.`evalAt` $(R_0$.`residue` $\bar g)$ the difference of that image and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$;
--   (W5) for $\zeta$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $f\in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $f\in F_0$: $f\in W_0$ if and only if `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $f\in W_0$;
--   (W6) (the model) there exist a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that the structure map sends $a\in A_b$ to the image of $a$ under $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`; $B$ is contained in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$, and every element $f$ of that compositum satisfies $f\,h=g$ for some $g,h\in B$ with $h\ne0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; the quotient of $B$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime; $f\in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ exactly when $f\,h=g$ for some $g,h\in B$ with the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$; the image of `jq` in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $B$; $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for all $\zeta$ and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; and, for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $\kappa[x_0,x_1]$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`) is a domain, and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field in the fraction field of `CoordRing q κ` of the group generated by the actions of the elements $(1,\zeta)$, $\zeta\in C_s$) with: $\#C_s = 2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M'` $s$, the latter being `jWidthChar q` of $s$.`evalAt` `jGeomGen` divided by `placeRamificationJ M'` $s$; the kernel of $\rho$ the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ compatible with the structure map, sending the image of $a\in A_b$ to the image of the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; every $z$ in the target a fraction $z\,\rho(h)=\rho(g)$ with $\rho(h)\ne0$ and $g,h\in B$; the range of $\rho$ consisting exactly of those $z$ whose image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of `CoordRing q κ`; and $\rho$ equivariant, in the sense that for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) and $f\in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` $f\in B$, the image of $\rho($`levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` $f)$ in the Drinfeld function field is obtained from that of $\rho(f)$ by [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at that element;
--   the following nine assertions hold for the pair $(F_0,W_0)$.
--
--   (C1) The compositum of the constants $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $F_0$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`, as in (F2). (C2) For $x\in k_0$: $x\in A$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$, as in (W1). (C3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring. (C4) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal. (C5) (residual transcendence) There exists $t\in W_0$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, then for every $n$ the image of the $n$-th coefficient of $p$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$. (C6) The clause (W4), verbatim. (C7) For every $\zeta$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, both that $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` and that, for $f\in F_0$ with image in $F_0$, membership of $f$ in $W_0$ is equivalent to membership of its image — the conjunction of (F3) and (W5). (C8) The linear disjointness clause (F4), verbatim. (C9) The model clause (W6), verbatim.
--
--   Thus the conclusion repeats the hypotheses on $(F_0,W_0)$, regrouping the two level-stability statements into a single clause, and adds the existence of the element $t$ of (C5).
--
--   This is the form, read on given data rather than through separate existential statements, of the construction of the semistable affine chart of the descended model of the full-level modular curve over a small constant field at a supersingular place in characteristic $q$, together with the identification of its special fibre with a quotient of the Drinfeld curve. The only clause of the conclusion not already among the hypotheses is the residual transcendence of some $t\in W_0$, which is supplied by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularDVR_residuallyTranscendental_of_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularDVR_residuallyTranscendental_of_affineChart). It feeds the all-in-one constructor [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_affineChart), which assembles charts and nodes on a single witness.
